This project contains an extraction of the author's H7 C++ TinyMPC task,
based on the algorithm
described in:

  K. Nguyen, S. Schoedel, A. Alavilli, B. Plancher and Z. Manchester,
  "TinyMPC: Model-Predictive Control on Resource-Constrained
  Microcontrollers," IEEE ICRA, 2024.

Original TinyMPC project: https://github.com/TinyMPC/TinyMPC
The upstream project is distributed under the MIT License.

This is not an official TinyMPC release. The extracted solver uses fitted
steady-state Riccati caches, not an exact finite-horizon recursion for arbitrary
terminal costs.

mpc/mcu/tinympc_task.cpp and its supporting solver/types/parameter table are
extracted from 2026_H7balanceHero/2026_H7NewFrame/TDT_Task and
TDT_Alg/tinympc_stm32/src. Board/global dependencies are replaced by explicit
inputs and platform hooks. Numeric coefficients and the original solver logic
are retained; empty coefficient arrays and one Eigen indexing expression are
adapted for standard C++ portability. The original cache-generation rho issue,
output scheduling, terminal approximation and lack of failure gating remain.
The new MATLAB export is not a drop-in replacement for the legacy sparse table.

Eigen is an external dependency, not vendored here. Eigen's own license applies
to Eigen. The existing copyright/license notice in the Eigen.h wrapper is kept.

The collision observer is extracted from the author's 2026_H7balanceHero
perception.cpp and MCG.m. See collision_detection/NOTICE for provenance,
extraction changes, and known legacy model issues.

No complete robot firmware, motor driver, communication protocol, PCB design,
or mechanical design is included in this repository.

